  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 AM CDT Fri Jul 3 2026\n\nThere will be a low chance for showers and thunderstorms across the \nCoastal Plains each afternoon through Saturday along the sea breeze. \nAs we head into next week, a mid-level ridge is expected to develop \nwhich will maintain our rain chances on the lower end. \n\nAbove normal temperature combining with ample low-level moisture \nwill promote  heat index values between 100-110 degrees through the \nweekend and into early next week. Please use caution if you are \nworking or playing outside or spending time outdoors for \nIndependence Day. Take plenty of breaks, drink water, and don't \nforget sunscreen (and mosquito repellent).\n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
